Step 4 of the build-up. Identical to virtualization-stacks-side-by-side-3.svg (see that prompt), with nothing
moved, plus the kernel half of the Linux/KVM box and its first VMM:

- The hypervisor row of box 1: /dev/kvm, labelled as the kvm module in Linux.
- Cloud Hypervisor as the leftmost VMM on top of it, connected to that row, and
  the VM it runs (with faded "ghost" VMs behind it, indicating that many VMs
  run side by side).

The other two VMM slots of that box stay empty.
